/* CUSTOM THEME OVERRIDES
 *
 * Add new GTK CSS rules below these examples. Remove the comment markers and
 * change the values to apply an override. Prefer the app-specific selectors
 * documented in the component index above to keep changes scoped.
 *
 * Example: recolor main app surfaces and text:
 *
 * window.background.card-window,
 * .magic-card,
 * .prompt-card,
 * .annotation-modal-card,
 * window.settings-window {
 *     color: @mp-foreground;
 *     background-color: @mp-background;
 * }
 *
 * Example: recolor the quick-action buttons:
 *
 * .prompt-chip,
 * .prompt-preset-btn {
 *     color: @mp-foreground;
 *     background-color: alpha(@mp-accent, 0.12);
 *     border-color: alpha(@mp-accent, 0.35);
 * }
 *
 * Example: use the accent color for interactive states:
 *
 * .prompt-chip:hover,
 * .prompt-annotate-btn:hover,
 * .annotation-tool-pill.active {
 *     color: @mp-accent;
 *     border-color: @mp-accent;
 * }
 *
 * Example: style response code blocks:
 *
 * .code-card {
 *     color: @mp-text;
 *     background-color: @mp-base;
 *     border-color: alpha(@mp-foreground, 0.24);
 * }
 *
 * GTK NOTES
 * - Use GTK-supported properties; CSS Grid, browser pseudo-elements, and
 *   browser custom properties are not available.
 * - GTK CSS values such as @theme_fg_color and alpha(color, opacity) are GTK
 *   syntax, not browser CSS syntax.
 * - The chat window's outer size, compositor opacity, blur, border, shadow,
 *   glow, and position are controlled by Hyprland settings, not GTK CSS.
 * - GTK CSS cannot change the image pixels drawn by the selection or
 *   annotation Cairo canvases.
 */
